{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.117.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-2236-libgcrypt20",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-2236 low vulnerability for libgcrypt20 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A timing-based side-channel flaw was found in libgcrypt's RSA implementation. This issue may allow a remote attacker to initiate a Bleichenbacher-style attack, which can lead to the decryption of RSA ciphertexts."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-2236",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-2236\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libgcrypt20\nVersion: 1.10.3-2ubuntu0.1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2024-2236](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-2236)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-2236**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libgcrypt20  | 1.10.3-2ubuntu0.1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2024-2236](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-2236)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libgcrypt20@1.10.3-2ubuntu0.1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11856-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11856 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Successfully using libcurl to do a transfer to a specific HTTP origin\n(`hostA`) with **Digest** authentication and then changing the origin to a\ndifferent one (`hostB`) for a second transfer, reusing the same handle, makes\nlibcurl wrongly pass on the  `Authorization:` header field meant for `hostA`,\nto `hostB`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11856",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.11\nFix Version: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.12\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-11856](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11856)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.11  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.12  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-11856](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11856)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.11?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11856-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11856 medium vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Successfully using libcurl to do a transfer to a specific HTTP origin\n(`hostA`) with **Digest** authentication and then changing the origin to a\ndifferent one (`hostB`) for a second transfer, reusing the same handle, makes\nlibcurl wrongly pass on the  `Authorization:` header field meant for `hostA`,\nto `hostB`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11856",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.11\nFix Version: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.12\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-11856](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11856)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4t64  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.11  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.12  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-11856](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11856)  |\n"
              },
