            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59843-libssh-4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59843 medium vulnerability for libssh-4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libssh. A remote authenticated peer can advertise a zero maximum packet size in SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN, causing later channel writes to loop indefinitely and consume CPU, leading to denial of service."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59843",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59843\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssh-4\nVersion: 0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-59843](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59843)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59843**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssh-4  | 0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-59843](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59843)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssh-4@0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=libssh"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59844-libssh-4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59844 medium vulnerability for libssh-4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libssh. A remote authenticated client can issue SSH_FXP_READ requests with an arbitrarily large length, causing a libssh SFTP server to allocate excessive memory and potentially exhaust it through repeated requests."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59844",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59844\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssh-4\nVersion: 0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-59844](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59844)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59844**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssh-4  | 0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-59844](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59844)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssh-4@0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=libssh"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9538-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9538 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.10 for Perl allow memory exhaustion via attacker controlled entry size field in tar header.\n\n_read_tar() reads each entry's payload with $handle-\u003eread($$data, $block), where $block is derived from the entry's 12-byte size field in the tar header with no upper bound on that value.\n\nA crafted header declaring a multi-gigabyte size causes Perl to allocate a scalar of that size."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-9538",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9538\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-9538](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-9538)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9538**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-9538](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-9538)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19487-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-19487 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions from 5.9.4 before 5.41.9 produce incorrect regular expression match results when a stale failure flag ends the Aho-Corasick prescan early in S_find_byclass.\n\nThe prescan walks the subject for positions where the full pattern could match, and the engine tries it from the leftmost one recorded. A failing transition sets the failed flag, and a later successful transition does not clear it, so the prescan reads the stale flag as a failure and stops before it can record a candidate that starts earlier. It takes a subject where one candidate is recorded and a later character then forces a fallback through a fail link that succeeds.\n\nExample:\n\n  \"ABCDE\" =~ m/ABCF|BCDE|C/;    # matches C at offset 2, not BCDE\n  \"ABCDE\" =~ m/ABCF|BCDE|C(G)/; # no match, BCDE missed\n\nAn alternation like this can miss input it should match, or match it on the wrong branch, so an access or filtering decision made from the result can be wrong."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19487",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19487\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-19487](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19487)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-19487**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-19487](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19487)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13221-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13221 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.43.9 produce silently incorrect regular expression matches when an alternation of more than 65535 fixed string branches is compiled into a trie in Perl_study_chunk.\n\nWhen such branches are combined into a trie, the delta between the first branch and the shared tail is stored in a 16-bit field. A branch count above 65535 overflows the field, and the trie's match decision table is truncated with no warning or error.\n\nA pattern of this shape produces false positive matches (matching strings it should not) and false negative matches (failing to match strings it should). When such a pattern gates an access or filtering decision, the result is wrong."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13221",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13221\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-13221](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13221)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-13221**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-13221](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13221)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42497-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42497 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.08 for Perl extract hardlinks to attacker controlled paths outside the extraction directory.\n\n_make_special_file() passes the tar header's linkname to link() without validating it against absolute paths or .. segments, creating a hardlink that shares the victim file's inode.\n\nA subsequent write through the extracted name modifies the victim file, and the post-extraction chmod, chown, and utime block in _extract_file() (guarded only against symlinks via -l) applies the tar header's mode, owner, and timestamps to the shared inode during extraction alone."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-42497",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-42497](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-42497)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-42497](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-42497)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-12087-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-12087 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Socket versions before 2.041 for Perl have an out-of-bounds heap read.\n\nIn Socket.xs, pack_ip_mreq_source() checks the length of its source argument before the argument is read, so the check tests the byte length carried over from the preceding multiaddr argument instead. Both addresses occupy a 4-byte field, so a valid multiaddr lets a source of any length pass the check, and the source is then copied into the 4-byte imr_sourceaddr field with a fixed-size copy. A source shorter than 4 bytes is not rejected, and the copy reads up to 3 bytes past the end of its buffer.\n\nCalling pack_ip_mreq_source() with a source value shorter than 4 bytes copies adjacent heap memory into the returned packed structure."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-12087",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-12087\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-12087](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-12087)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-12087**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-12087](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-12087)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48959-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-48959 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IO::Uncompress::Unzip versions before 2.220 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via per-byte read loop in fastForward.\n\nfastForward() compares length $offset (the digit count of the offset, 1 to 19) against the chunk size $c instead of $offset itself, so $c shrinks from 16 KiB to 1-19 bytes per iteration.\n\nExtracting a named entry from an attacker supplied zip via IO::Uncompress::Unzip-\u003enew($zip, Name =\u003e $target) drives a per-byte read loop scaling with the entry's compressed size, up to the non-Zip64 4 GiB cap."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48959",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48959\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-48959](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48959)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48959**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-48959](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48959)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57433-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57433 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Storable versions before 3.41 for Perl have a signed integer overflow when deserializing a crafted SX_HOOK record.\n\nretrieve_hook_common reads a signed 32-bit item count from an SX_HOOK record and calls av_extend with that count plus one. A count of I32_MAX wraps the addition to a negative value.\n\nA crafted blob passed to thaw or retrieve triggers the overflow; av_extend receives the negative count and dies with a panic, terminating the deserialization."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-57433",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-57433\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-57433](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-57433)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-57433**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-57433](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-57433)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59850-libssh-4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59850 medium vulnerability for libssh-4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libssh. If data packets are processed after a channel is closed, channel data callbacks can be invoked after the associated data has already been freed, leading to crashes or possible use-after-free conditions."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59850",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59850\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssh-4\nVersion: 0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-59850](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59850)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59850**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssh-4  | 0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-59850](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-59850)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssh-4@0.10.6-2ubuntu0.4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=libssh"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59847-libssh-4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59847 medium vulnerability for libssh-4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libssh. Incorrect AES-GCM finalization checks in builds using the OpenSSL backend can effectively remove integrity protection, allowing an in-path attacker to modify plaintext on the wire without detection."
              },
