            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15534-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15534 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.45.1 have out-of-bounds heap reads and writes during regular expression matching via an undersized superlinear cache in S_regmatch.\n\nThe regex engine's superlinear cache holds one bit per subject position for each participating WHILEM node, so the bit count is the subject length plus one times the number of nodes. Nothing checks that product for positive overflow of the signed 32-bit count: a 286331153 byte subject matched against a pattern with 15 participating nodes stores the count as 14, leaving a two byte cache. The cache is then indexed from the real match position and node number, so reads go past the end of the allocation, and on failure CACHEsayNO sets a bit past it.\n\nA caller that matches an attacker controlled subject of this size against a pattern of this shape can crash the process or corrupt heap memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-15534",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-15534](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-15534)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-15534](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-15534)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15370-libssh-4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15370 medium vulnerability for libssh-4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libssh. During SFTP server directory listing, the longname field is constructed with unsafe concatenation into a fixed-size stack buffer. When a client causes the server to list attacker-controlled filenames, sufficiently long names can overflow that stack buffer and may lead to crashes or possible code execution on the server."
              },
